    createStaticVNode('<h1 id="_3-xarm-1s-pc-software-and-app-learning" tabindex="-1">3.xArm 1S PC Software and APP Learning <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-xarm-1s-pc-software-and-app-learning" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.xArm 1S PC Software and APP Learning&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="_3-1-pc-software-instruction" tabindex="-1">3.1 PC Software Instruction <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-1-pc-software-instruction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.1 PC Software Instruction&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_3-1-1-software-installation" tabindex="-1">3.1.1 Software Installation <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-1-1-software-installation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.1.1 Software Installation&quot;">​</a></h3><p><strong>Step 1：</strong>Please get the installation pack in this file and click to download.</p><p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Choose the language and click “<strong>OK</strong>”.</p><img loading="lazy" height="162" width="349" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_0 + '" style="width:800px;"><p><strong>Step3:</strong> &quot;<strong>Create desktop shortcut</strong>&quot; is automatically checked by default, and then click &quot;<strong>Next</strong>&quot;.</p><img loading="lazy" height="415" width="582" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_1 + '" style="width:800px;"><p><strong>Step4:</strong> Wait for the installation and click “<strong>Finish</strong>”.</p><img loading="lazy" height="415" width="582" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_2 + '" style="width:800px;"><h3 id="_3-1-2-device-connection" tabindex="-1">3.1.2 Device Connection <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-1-2-device-connection" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.1.2 Device Connection&quot;">​</a></h3><p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Connect the power adapter to the robotic arm and turn on the switch.</p><p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Connect the micro-USB cable to the USB serial port on the controller and the USB port in the computer.</p><img loading="lazy" height="767" width="1150" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_3 + '" style="width:800px;"><p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The software will automatically connect after the xArm 1S is turned on. When connected successfully, the red icon will turn green.</p><h3 id="_3-1-3-function-instruction" tabindex="-1">3.1.3 Function Instruction <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-1-3-function-instruction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.1.3 Function Instruction&quot;">​</a></h3><img loading="lazy" height="760" width="1260" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_4 + '" style="width:800px;"><p>① Device connected:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:center;">Icon</th><th style="text-align:left;">Function</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:center;"><img loading="lazy" height="58" width="64" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_5 + '" style="width:100px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Display connection status. When successfully connected, it is in green. It will be in red when not connected or disconnected.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>② Servo operation:</p><p>Drag the slider to adjust the position of the corresponding servo.</p><img loading="lazy" height="100" width="131" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_6 + '" style="width:300px;"><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:center;">Icon</th><th style="text-align:left;">Function</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:center;"><img loading="lazy" height="99" width="131" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_7 + '" style="width:300px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Servo ID number. Take servo 2 as an example.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;"><img loading="lazy" height="100" width="131" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_6 + '" style="width:300px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Adjust the servo position from 0 to 1000.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;"><img loading="lazy" height="100" width="131" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_6 + '" style="width:300px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Adjust servo deviation from -100 to 100.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>③ Action details list:</p><p>The action details list displays the running time of the current action and the data of each servo.</p><img loading="lazy" height="106" width="699" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_8 + '" style="width:800px;"><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:center;">Icon</th><th style="text-align:left;">Function</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:center;"><img loading="lazy" height="23" width="68" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_9 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Number of action group. There are 230 action groups in total, and each action group can hold up to 1020 actions. If it exceeds, it will be prompted that it can only be run online and cannot be downloaded.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;"><img loading="lazy" height="21" width="68" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_10 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Running time.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;"><img loading="lazy" height="21" width="48" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_11 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">ID value of the corresponding servo. Double click <img loading="lazy" height="16" width="77" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_12 + '" style="width:200px;"> to revise the value.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>④ Action group setting:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Icon</th><th style="text-align:left;">Function</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="229" width="201" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_13 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Select action group number from 0-230. No.0 is set as “Attention” action by default.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="229" width="201" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_13 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Download the actions in the current list to the controller. The original actions will be overwritten after downloading.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="229" width="201" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_13 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">（Be careful）Click to delete all the data of action groups from 0 to 230.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="229" width="201" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_13 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Run the selected action once.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="229" width="201" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_13 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Stop the running action group.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="56" width="166" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_14 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Add the action after adjusting the servo value.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="50" width="170" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_15 + '" style="width:800px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Delete the selected action in the action list.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="56" width="167" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_16 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Replace the angle value selected in the action details list. Action time (ms)</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="56" width="177" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_17 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Insert the new action on the action list. Action time (ms)）</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="81" width="163" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_18 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Click to choose the action group, then add it to the action list. The action group can be found in the provided folder “Appendix/Action Group”.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="70" width="157" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_19 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Save the current actions in the action list into the computer.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="71" width="156" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_20 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Click to integrate the provided action groups.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="164" width="170" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_21 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Click to run the action group in the current action list（Choose the “Loop” to repeat the actions.)</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="58" width="170" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_22 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">All the servos are back to the middle position.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="52" width="167" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_23 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Click to loosen the joints of the robotic arm, and then change the stance of robotic arm manually.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="54" width="171" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_24 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td style="text-align:left;">Read the angle data from the manual programming.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>⑤ Servo setting:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Icon</th><th>Function</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="42" width="96" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_25 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td>Set language.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="56" width="165" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_26 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td>Read the deviation saved in the controller automatically.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="60" width="153" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_27 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td>After clicking, the deviation adjusted by the PC software can be downloaded to the robotic arm.</td></tr><tr><td><img loading="lazy" height="54" width="155" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_28 + '" style="width:200px;"></td><td>Click to delete the deviation on the PC software, but the data saved by the control board will not change.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="_3-2-action-programming" tabindex="-1">3.2 Action Programming <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-2-action-programming" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.2 Action Programming&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Project Outcome</strong></li></ol><p>Program an action group consisting of 9 actions to allow the xArm 1S to grip.</p><p>(Note: The action programmed in this section is only for programming learning. If you need the standard actions, please go to the folder &quot;<strong>Appendix/Action Group</strong>&quot;.)</p><ol start="2"><li><strong>Complete Program</strong></li></ol><h3 id="_3-2-1-action-programming" tabindex="-1">3.2.1 Action Programming <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-2-1-action-programming" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.2.1 Action Programming&quot;">​</a></h3><p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Turn on the robotic arm and connect to the computer. Double-click to open the PC software.</p><p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Click “<strong>Action File</strong>” to open the provided folder and select No.0 action group. Click “<strong>Run-online</strong>” to update the servo data on the left side, which is the first action.</p><img loading="lazy" height="760" width="1260" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_29 + '" style="width:800px;"><p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Program the robotic arm to bend forward and open the gripper. Drag the sliders of servos of ID1, 3, 4, 5 to the value as shown in the figure:</p><img loading="lazy" height="550" width="544" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_30 + '" style="width:500px;"><p>Hold down the left mouse button and quickly click the slider to make fine adjustments.</p><p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Click “<strong>Add Action</strong>” to add the second action to the list.</p><img loading="lazy" height="302" width="706" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_31 + '" style="width:800px;"><p><strong>Step 5:</strong> Lower the robotic arm a little bit and make fine adjustment of the gripper, which is the preparation for the next step of gripping. Please drag the servos of ID 1, 3, and 4 to the value in the figure.</p><img loading="lazy" height="581" width="541" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_32 + '" style="width:500px;"><p><strong>Step 6:</strong> Set the gripper to close. Do not forget to add the fourth action to the list.</p><img loading="lazy" height="553" width="535" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_33 + '" style="width:500px;"><p><strong>Step 7:</strong> Hold the block and then raise the arm. Please adjust the position of servo 5.</p><img loading="lazy" height="563" width="535" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_34 + '" style="width:500px;"><p><strong>Step 8:</strong> Adjust the servo 6 to rotate the base.</p><img loading="lazy" height="577" width="541" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_35 + '" style="width:500px;"><p><strong>Step 9:</strong> After reaching the designated position, lower the robotic arm and open the gripper to put down the block.</p><img loading="lazy" height="560" width="542" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_36 + '" style="width:500px;"><p><strong>Step 10:</strong> Release the gripper and then put down the block.</p><img loading="lazy" height="553" width="542" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_37 + '" style="width:500px;"><p><strong>Step 11:</strong> Set the robotic arm to the initial position. Right-click the No.1 action, select “<strong>Copy,</strong>” and then right-click the No.8 action to paste it.</p><img loading="lazy" height="321" width="695" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_38 + '" style="width:800px;"><h3 id="_3-2-2-download-action-group" tabindex="-1">3.2.2 Download Action Group <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-2-2-download-action-group" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.2.2 Download Action Group&quot;">​</a></h3><p><strong>Step 1:</strong> After programming, please save the action group to your computer for later debugging. Click “<strong>Save action file</strong>” and fill in the file name, then save it (see example below ).</p><img loading="lazy" height="578" width="1249" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_39 + '" style="width:800px;"><p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Download the action group into xArm 1S. Select a number and click <img loading="lazy" height="53" width="193" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_40 + '" style="width:200px;">button to download. There will be a beep sound if succeed in downloading the action group.</p><img loading="lazy" height="228" width="198" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_41 + '" style="width:400px;"><h2 id="_3-3-app-custom-control" tabindex="-1">3.3 APP Custom Control <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-3-app-custom-control" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.3 APP Custom Control&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Project Outcome</strong></li></ol><p>Perform the action group file “<strong>No.20</strong>” edited in this unit “<strong>Lesson 2 Action Editing Teaching</strong>” by the custom function of the mobile APP.</p><ol start="2"><li><strong>Complete Program</strong></li></ol><h3 id="_3-3-1-confirm-work" tabindex="-1">3.3.1 Confirm Work <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-3-1-confirm-work" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.3.1 Confirm Work&quot;">​</a></h3><p>1) Confirm that the app Bluetooth and GPS are turned on.</p><p>2) Confirm that the No.20 action group has been successfully downloaded to the robot arm controller. The download is successful, and the PC software will prompt.</p><h3 id="_3-3-2-preparation" tabindex="-1">3.3.2 Preparation <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-3-2-preparation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.3.2 Preparation&quot;">​</a></h3><p><strong>Step1:</strong> Turn on the robot arm switch, and then open the app “<strong>Wonderbot</strong>”.</p><p><strong>Step2:</strong> According to the content “<strong>2. Handle Games Learning-&gt;Lesson 2 Mobile phone APP control</strong>”, connect the device.</p><p><strong>Step3:</strong> Enter the xArm remote control interface, click the “<strong>Action Groups</strong> ” button on the main interface, and click &quot;<strong>Add</strong>&quot; in the pop-up.</p><img loading="lazy" height="706" width="1268" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_42 + '" style="width:600px;"><p><strong>Step4:</strong> Fill in the action group name and action group in the pop-up dialog box.</p><p>The action group name can be filled in arbitrarily, but the action group number must be filled in correctly, otherwise it cannot be realized.</p><img loading="lazy" height="712" width="1265" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_43 + '" style="width:00px;"><img loading="lazy" height="712" width="1265" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_44 + '" style="width:800px;"><p><strong>Step 5:</strong> After adding, click the action group name to execute it once.</p><img loading="lazy" height="712" width="1265" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_45 + '" style="width:800px;"><p><strong>Step6:</strong> If you need to modify or delete an action group, slide or long-press the action name button and click “<strong>Delete</strong>”.</p><h2 id="_3-4-integrate-action-files" tabindex="-1">3.4 Integrate Action Files <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-4-integrate-action-files" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.4 Integrate Action Files&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_3-4-1-project-outcome" tabindex="-1">3.4.1 Project Outcome <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-4-1-project-outcome" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.4.1 Project Outcome&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Learn the robot arm Integrate action groups function, and realize the merging between action groups.</p><h3 id="_3-4-2-complete-program" tabindex="-1">3.4.2 Complete Program <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-4-2-complete-program" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.4.2 Complete Program&quot;">​</a></h3><p><strong>Step1:</strong> Turn on the PC software, connect the serial port software, click action group setting area “Integrate file” button, open No.1 action group “<strong>5.Appendix-&gt;Action group</strong>”.</p><img loading="lazy" height="755" width="1107" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_46 + '" style="width:800px;"><p><strong>Step2:</strong> Now, we see that the No.1 action group parameter is shown in the action group details list.</p><img loading="lazy" height="292" width="704" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_47 + '" style="width:800px;"><p><strong>Step3:</strong> Click the “<strong>serial Action group</strong>” button again, and select the No.2 action group file for series connection.</p><img loading="lazy" height="437" width="1083" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_48 + '" style="width:800px;"><p><strong>Step 4:</strong> We can click “<strong>Run Online</strong>” button to run the new action group in series online.</p><img loading="lazy" height="760" width="1260" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_49 + '" style="width:800px;"><p><strong>Step5:</strong> Click the” Save Action File” button to save the new series connection action group for later debugging. Here we name it ”121 Rotation ”.</p><img loading="lazy" height="583" width="1260" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_50 + '" style="width:800px;"><p><strong>Step 6:</strong> If the action details list exceeds 1020 actions in serial, the PC software will prompt that the limit is exceeded. In this case, the action group can not be downloaded to the controller and only can be run and checked on line.</p><img loading="lazy" height="760" width="1260" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_51 + '" style="width:800px;"><h2 id="_3-5-offline-run-learning" tabindex="-1">3.5 Offline Run Learning <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-5-offline-run-learning" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.5 Offline Run Learning&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_3-5-1-project-outcome" tabindex="-1">3.5.1 Project Outcome <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-5-1-project-outcome" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.5.1 Project Outcome&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Control the robotic arm by pressing the offline running button instead of the software control.</p><h3 id="_3-5-2-complete-program" tabindex="-1">3.5.2 Complete Program <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-5-2-complete-program" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.5.2 Complete Program&quot;">​</a></h3><p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Connect the computer and robotic arm controller by USB wire, and turn on the PC software.</p><p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Open an action group file arbitrarily (&quot;<strong>5. Appendix -&gt; Action Group File</strong>&quot;), such as &quot;<strong>No. 4-Show Action 2</strong>&quot;.</p><p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Set the action group number to 100 and then click on the “<strong>Download</strong>” button. If wanna run offline, you should download it into the No. 100 Action group because the No.100 operation group is set to run offline by default.</p><img loading="lazy" height="235" width="201" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_52 + '" style="width:400px;"><p><strong>Step 4:</strong> After the action group download is complete, the PC software interface will pop up a prompt box indicating that the download is successful. Click the &quot;<strong>OK</strong>&quot; button to close the prompt box to complete.</p><img loading="lazy" height="760" width="1260" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_53 + '" style="width:800px;"><p><strong>Step 5:</strong> Turn on the power, and then press the 【<strong>Run】</strong>button on the controller to run the No.100 action group offline. Long press button for 3 seconds, and the action group will be executed repeatedly.</p><img loading="lazy" height="767" width="1150" class="common_img" src="' + _imports_54 + '" style="width:800px;">', 111)
